A1. You'll find these right under your nose. ~ CROSSWORDS
A10. A brief afternoon. ~ AFT
A13. This's what Gandhi's followers work for. ~ RUPEE
A14. Many a good bangup party has been spoiled by this kind of punch. ~ FOUL
A15. Singly this sounds mushy; doubly, nutty. ~ COO
A16. The work of the stone man. ~ MASONRY
A18. This is back of that wet or dry issue. ~ WEATHER
A20. Eye-catchers. ~ ADS
A21. Anyway, Rudy Vallee will never sing this. ~ DUET
A23. This's very helpful to wire-walkers and society ladies. ~ POISE
A24. Another thing that goes over the modern girl's head. ~ SLIP
A26. A cover-up agent. ~ MASK
A28. Yes, it's I. ~ ME
A29. Seals. ~ SEALS
A31. Donged. ~ RANG
A33. Aye. ~ EVER
A36. What girls who will have none of this and none of that eventually become. ~ NUNS
A38. One thing you can safely bring up during a battle. ~ REAR
A40. This causes swelling of the head. ~ EGO
A41. Where you go when you take a lift in London. ~ UP
A43. There have been lots of new bawls about this lately. ~ GOLF
A45. Dora thinks this is a well-fed boys' school. ~ ETON
